{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-topological-mass-upper-bound","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:topological-mass-upper-bound","kind":"proposition","title":"Upper bound for the topological decomposition of mass","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-mass-identity","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-brane-boundary","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-descent-eigenspaces"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-topological-mass-categorical","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-topological-mass"],"tags":["mass","topological-decomposition","descent-involution","upper-bound"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Torsion.mass_upper_bound_localised","text":"topological-mass-upper-bound.md","leanSource":"topological-mass-upper-bound.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:topological-mass-upper-bound\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe (<a href=\"#def:quantum-observable-universe\" data-at=\"quantum-observable-universes/qou-definition\">quantum observable universe</a>). Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varrho \\colon \\mathbf{1} \\to A</code> be a closed cycle (<a href=\"#def:mass-identity\" data-at=\"mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-opener/mass-endomorphism-mass-identity\">mass identity</a>) whose categorical support is generated by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N</code> consecutive extensions along the brane tower (<a href=\"#def:recursive-brane-tower\" data-at=\"lifting-and-descent/jet-prolongation\">recursive brane tower</a>) from a base-level morphism <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varrho_0 \\colon \\mathbf{1} \\to A_0</code>. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{tr}_{\\mathrm{desc}}(\\varrho)</code> be the trace restricted to the descended subalgebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{im}\\,\\hat{\\tau}_n</code>, and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{tr}_{\\mathrm{trans}}(\\varrho, p_i)</code> be the trace restricted to the component of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ker\\hat{\\tau}_n</code> localised at the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">i</code>-th blow-up centre <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p_i</code> (<a href=\"#def:brane-boundary\" data-at=\"lifting-and-descent/descent\">brane boundary</a>). Then</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathfrak{m}(\\varrho)\n  \\le\n  \\bigl\\lVert \\mathrm{tr}_{\\mathrm{desc}}(\\varrho) \\bigr\\rVert +\n  \\sum_{i=1}^{N}\n  \\bigl\\lVert \\mathrm{tr}_{\\mathrm{trans}}(\\varrho, p_i) \\bigr\\rVert .</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-upper-bound.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"11.1.16","page":"b/prop-topological-mass-upper-bound","qa":{"counts":{"pass":0,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":0,"unknown":0,"stale":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.LiftingDescent.Torsion.mass_upper_bound_localised","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-upper-bound.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
